From: stateful-audio <noreply@moises>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: [PATCH 0009] libavcodec/aac: AAC decoder state snapshot/restore

Mirror of Phase 3's encoder state APIs (patches 0002 + 0003) for the
native AAC decoder. Adds:

  - libavcodec/aac/aacdec_state.{c,h} — FFSA writer/reader for the
    minimal AAC-LC cross-frame state set: the per-SCE IMDCT overlap
    buffer (saved[1536]), is_saved flag, window_sequence[0..1],
    use_kb_window[0..1], and the PNS random_state.

  - avcodec_{get,set}_decoder_state public API in libavcodec/avcodec.h
    and libavcodec/decode.c. Switch-on-codec-id routes AAC_CODEC_ID_AAC
    to ff_aac_decoder_{get,set}_state; all other codecs return ENOSYS.

  - New FFSA component id 0x0004 (AAC_DECODER) and atom tags 0x3001..
    0x3005 in libavcodec/state_format.h.

Library validation: stateful-aac-validation/test-harness/
aac_decoder_bit_exact_test passes on all 6 Moises stems (vocals, bass,
drums, guitars, piano, other) at chunks ∈ {4, 8, 16, 32, 40} —
30/30 bit-exact match between a continuous decoder reference and a
chunked decoder with state transferred at every chunk boundary.

This closes the last identified drift source in the nginx-vod-module
pipeline (Phase 27 proved encoder + amix + aresample state transfer
were bit-exact; Phase 27 pipeline oracle isolated the remaining
audible residual to source AAC decoder cold-start; Phase 28 fixes
that).

Depends on: 0001-state-format-framework.patch (shared FFSA writer/
reader helpers and the state_format.h component-id namespace).

